The bug is that the goroutines capture the loop variable `i` by reference. In Go 1.21, a single `i` variable is reused for each iteration, so by the time each goroutine runs, the loop has already finished and `i` is `5`.

Fix the data race by passing the current loop value into the goroutine:

<solution language="go" verdict="fix">
package main

import (
    "fmt"
    "sync"
)

func main() {
    var wg sync.WaitGroup
    for i := 0; i < 5; i++ {
        wg.Add(1)
        go func(n int) {
            defer wg.Done()
            fmt.Println(n)
        }(i)
    }
    wg.Wait()
}
</solution>

