The bug is this line:

```javascript
const city = order.shipping_address.city;
```

It assumes `order.shipping_address` always exists. If a production order is missing `shipping_address` (or `order` itself is undefined), then `order.shipping_address.city` crashes with:

```text
Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'city')
```

It likely works on your machine only because your local test data always includes a shipping address.

Fix: use optional chaining so missing values fall through to the default.

<solution language="javascript" verdict="fix">
function getShippingZone(order) {
    const city = order?.shipping_address?.city;
    const zones = {
        "New York": "east",
        "Los Angeles": "west",
        "Chicago": "central",
    };
    return zones[city] || "standard";
}
</solution>

